        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "f2dd6788-d84d-5409-9f83-3bff19c554b8",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Companies: Rendezvous Music, Mack Avenue Records\n- People: Dave Koz, Frank Cody, Hyman Katz, Kirk Whalum, Jonathan Butler, Kyle Eastwood, Wayman Tisdale\n- Places: University of Oklahoma\n- Roles: record label founders, musician, radio entrepreneur, music business veteran, NBA player, bass guitarist\n- Topics: record labels, music releases, college basketball honors\n\nFacts:\n- Rendezvous Music, formerly known as Rendezvous Entertainment, was founded in 2002 by Dave Koz, Frank Cody, and Hyman Katz.\n- In August 2008, Rendezvous Music became part of the Mack Avenue Records label group.\n- Rendezvous Music continues to release new music by Kirk Whalum, Jonathan Butler, and Kyle Eastwood.\n- Rendezvous Music also released previously unreleased music by Wayman Tisdale.\n- Wayman Tisdale was born on June 9, 1964, and died on May 15, 2009.\n- Wayman Tisdale was an American NBA player and a smooth jazz bass guitarist.\n- Wayman Tisdale was a three-time All-American at the University of Oklahoma.\n- Wayman Tisdale was elected to the National Collegiate Basketball Hall of Fame in 2009.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
